      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey im studying for my security+ and im a bit stuck. if i am already hashing a password, why do i actually need to add a salt to it? wouldnt the hash alone be enough to keep it secure?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A hash alone is vulnerable if two users have the same password, as their hashes would be identical. Salts ensure that even identical passwords produce unique, unpredictable hash outputs by adding random data before hashing. This prevents attackers from using precomputed rainbow tables or easily predicting hash collisions to crack multiple accounts at once.",
      "source": "target",
